# Modelfile: Qwen3.6-35B-A3B, 64K context — "64k-agentic" tuning, the
# recommended floor for agentic CLI use (Copilot CLI, opencode) via BYOK/
# Ollama. "Agentic" here means tool-calling/multi-step-action use, as
# opposed to plain single-turn chat.
#
# Why 64K and not 32K: Copilot CLI's own static overhead (system prompt +
# all built-in tool schemas — bash, edit, view, grep, glob, task, plus the
# GitHub MCP server) measured at ~21,504 input tokens for a trivial "hi"
# prompt, *before* any real conversation. That alone is 65% of a 32K window,
# leaving no realistic room for conversation + output. A 64K window leaves
# ~44K after that static floor — comfortable for a coding/agentic session.
#
# Same output-truncation fix as qwen3.6__35b-a3b-32k-standalone/Modelfile:
#   - num_predict capped at 16384 (not -1/unbounded) so generation always
#     stops on its own terms with tokens returned, instead of riding
#     "thinking" all the way to num_ctx with nothing visible.
#   - SYSTEM prompt nudges concise thinking + guarantees a final answer.
# See docs/tuning-results.md for the full reasoning and empirical tests
# behind both choices.

FROM qwen3.6:35b-a3b

PARAMETER num_ctx 65536
# num_gpu intentionally omitted — host-wide OLLAMA_NUM_GPU/OLLAMA_MAX_VRAM
# env vars already handle GPU offload; a static value here conflicts with it.
PARAMETER num_batch 256
PARAMETER num_thread 16

PARAMETER temperature 0.7
PARAMETER top_p 0.9

PARAMETER num_predict 16384

SYSTEM """You are a helpful assistant. Keep your internal reasoning
efficient and proportional to the difficulty of the question — do not
over-deliberate on simple requests. Regardless of how much you have
reasoned, always make sure to produce a clear, complete final answer
before you finish; if you notice you are running low on room to respond,
wrap up your reasoning early and give your best answer rather than leaving
it incomplete.
"""
